OL,3,GNEWSAExperts identify new apple from
OL,4,Adecades-old tree
OL,5,
OL,6,FA previously unidentified apple variety
OL,7,Fgrown in a back garden was discovered
OL,8,Fafter a donation of surplus fruit.
OL,10,FThe apple was found on Clarendon Road
OL,11,Fin High Town in Luton in 2023, where a
OL,12,Ftree believed to be between 70 and 90
OL,13,Fyears old had been growing for decades.
OL,15,FIt was tested by the National Institute
OL,16,Fof Agricultural Botany in Cambridge
OL,17,Flast year and compared against
OL,18,Fthousands of other UK and European
OL,19,Fvarieties.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
